{
  "summary": "The rejection flow from final-human-approval has two significant gaps that explain why nothing changes when items are re-processed. First, the web UI's reject button (index.html:574-579) sends a move request with only target_stage='rejected' but no rejection reason field - the user's feedback is never captured or stored. The move handler in tui.py:2168 only records a generic 'Moved via web UI' history entry. Second, items land in the 'rejected' stage which is terminal (no auto-processing), and when manually moved back to 'implementing', the pipeline restarts without any context about why it was rejected. By contrast, the automated review loop works correctly: plan_reviews and impl_reviews store structured feedback that gets injected into prompts via fix-feedback.md and plan-headless.md templates. To fix this, two changes are needed: (1) the rejection UI and API must capture a rejection reason and store it as an impl_review entry with verdict='FAIL' and the user's feedback, and (2) when an item re-enters the pipeline from rejected/final-human-approval, the latest rejection feedback must be passed to the agent via the existing fix-feedback prompt mechanism, just like automated review failures are handled today."
